rt 8080 on lan-b) on TCP port 80 of node2's transit address\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"OPNsense (node2) was given a transit interface opt1=10.0.23.2/24 and a destination-NAT rdr rule (tcp/80 -> 10.0.24.2:8080) plus an associated pf pass rule (initially misconfigured to match the pre-NAT destination, then corrected to match the translated destination 10.0.24.2:8080). Verified working via pfctl -sr output showing the pass rule and multiple successful curl requests to http://10.0.23.2:80/ that returned node4's service body ('node4-service-ok'), both before and after node2's restart.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-5f420a3c283c4856\",\"cmd-ea6a8c2e25bf4022\",\"cmd-5b8bd04e05894f26\",\"cmd-738c5a5e54d440cb\",\"cmd-720aaa7d8e3c4392\",\"cmd-2c38c192d3f74b71\",\"cmd-a327cacf45f74526\",\"cmd-07bd0dbbe9db4740\",\"cmd-1b7f0f0f5f594629\"]},{\"id\":\"node1-route-to-transit\",\"requirement\":\"Give node1 a route to node2's transit address\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"node1 (VyOS) eth1 was configured with 10.0.23.1/24, the same subnet as node2's transit address (10.0.23.2), committed and saved. The resulting kernel routing table on node1 shows a connected route '10.0.23.0/24 dev eth1 proto kernel scope link src 10.0.23.1', satisfying the reachability requirement; this route persisted through node1's restart.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-8c304cfa7af040e5\",\"cmd-fcd9776d639e43e4\",\"cmd-8b5b744f49874a92\"]},{\"id\":\"node3-indirect-access\",\"requirement\":\"node3 on lan-a reaches the service by addressing node2's transit address rather than node4 directly\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"node3 was given a persistent static route to 10.0.23.0/24 via node1 (10.0.12.1). Multiple curl requests from node3 to http://10.0.23.2:80/ (node2's transit address, never node4's address) succeeded and returned node4's content, confirming the indirect access path both pre- and post-restart of every node.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-9ec4f593b5fa4bff\",\"cmd-2c38c192d3f74b71\",\"cmd-a327cacf45f74526\",\"cmd-e460c78e23454cdc\",\"cmd-28d590836a2c4387\",\"cmd-31d9dfd903124d7f\"]},{\"id\":\"node4-service-precondition\",\"requirement\":\"node4 must actually be running the HTTP service on 8080 for the publish/route work to have any effect\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"No HTTP service was found listening on node4:8080 initially; the executor created and enabled a persistent systemd unit (python2 SimpleHTTPServer) and opened firewalld port 8080. Verified active with a local curl returning content, and again after node4's restart, plus the after_executor lifecycle snapshot shows tcp *:8080 listening (python2, pid 926).\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-e90b836857314cad\",\"cmd-1c5b86f6ce8f412e\",\"cmd-7e13bd7eeec8439a\",\"cmd-f3b404e3ea6c41c6\"]},{\"id\":\"restart-node1\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide node-restart evidence protocol: node1\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Healthy pre-restart baseline (boot_id 32669db3, addressing 10.0.23.1/10.0.12.1) was captured, reboot issued and acknowledged, a distinct post-restart boot_id (b5fb3ab0) confirmed, and full recovery of interface addressing, routing, and ip_forward verified, plus a successful end-to-end curl from node3. Cross-checked against the fixed global lifecycle snapshots, which show the same boot_id transition.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-55e48e301fd84c83\",\"cmd-ca438d5f44b34376\",\"cmd-d5fcf8b714174df3\",\"cmd-8b5b744f49874a92\",\"cmd-3af9eef82cfc45be\"]},{\"id\":\"restart-node2\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide node-restart evidence protocol: node2\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Healthy pre-restart baseline (kern.boottime 05:42:38) captured, reboot issued, a distinct post-restart boottime (06:04:07) confirmed, and full recovery of opt1/opt2 addressing, static route, NAT rdr rule, and filter rule verified along with a successful end-to-end curl from node3. Consistent with the fixed global lifecycle snapshot boottime transition.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-320e89992cab49de\",\"cmd-09153f4b7fcf4e61\",\"cmd-4c09610c5ba2465b\",\"cmd-1b7f0f0f5f594629\",\"cmd-e460c78e23454cdc\"]},{\"id\":\"restart-node3\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide node-restart evidence protocol: node3\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Healthy pre-restart baseline (boot_id 809708f3) captured, sudo reboot issued, a distinct post-restart boot_id (4371b46f) confirmed, and recovery of eth1 addressing, static route, and successful curl to node2's transit address verified. Matches the fixed global lifecycle snapshot boot_id transition.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-e684013bb8f2436f\",\"cmd-a407003d49dd42f0\",\"cmd-460b9c5fa3f9498f\",\"cmd-28d590836a2c4387\"]},{\"id\":\"restart-node4\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide node-restart evidence protocol: node4\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Healthy pre-restart baseline (boot_id d72bd4ec) captured, sudo reboot issued, a distinct post-restart boot_id (8d01b152) confirmed, and recovery of eth1 addressing, node4-http.service active state, firewalld port 8080, and end-to-end curl from node3 verified. Matches the fixed global lifecycle snapshot boot_id transition and post-executor listening-socket state showing python2 on :8080.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-64397c06e5f84f67\",\"cmd-d1fe48da869f4cef\",\"cmd-66e25dd5df9741f5\",\"cmd-f3b404e3ea6c41c6\",\"cmd-31d9dfd903124d7f\"]}],\"confidence\":0.9,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.75,\"summary\":\"The bulk of the executor's work was legitimate discovery (the wiring topology was undocumented) and necessary configuration/troubleshooting, most of which was fully reverted. Extensive temporary IP aliasing used to empirically determine L2 wiring on node1 (eth1/eth2), node2 (vtnet1/vtnet2), node3 (eth1), and node4 (eth1) was later flushed/removed (cmd-2ccc93d5b09a4eaf, cmd-ec35a46e7f9b4fdf, cmd-0ef69da5a1f04323, cmd-a14f86aee180426f) - a bounded, reverted mutation used as a necessary prerequisite, not penalized heavily. However, the executor's after_executor lifecycle snapshot for